{"tool_name":"ionflow","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"ionflow","home":"https://github.com/wanchanglin/ionflow","license":"Not licensed","summary":"Galaxy tool for processing and analysis of ionomics data , based on the modification of R package IonFlow.","addition_date":"2022-02-24T15:17:37.853728Z","last_update_date":"2022-02-24T15:17:37.856316Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Script"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:ionflow","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"j.iacovacci@imperial.ac.uk","name":"J. Iacovacci","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1430-5062","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"r.glen@imperial.ac.uk","name":"R. C. Glen","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"J. L. Griffin"},{"name":"W. Lin"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Essential dynamics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3891"},{"term":"Gene-set enrichment analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2436"},{"term":"Principal component analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3960"},{"term":"Principal component visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2939"}]}],"name":"IonFlow","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1007/S11306-021-01841-Z","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2021, The Author(s).Introduction: Inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometry (ICP-MS) experiments generate complex multi-dimensional data sets that require specialist data analysis tools. Objective: Here we describe tools to facilitate analysis of the ionome composed of high-throughput elemental profiling data. Methods: IonFlow is a Galaxy tool written in R for ionomics data analysis and is freely accessible at https://github.com/wanchanglin/ionflow. It is designed as a pipeline that can process raw data to enable exploration and interpretation using multivariate statistical techniques and network-based algorithms, including principal components analysis, hierarchical clustering, relevance network extraction and analysis, and gene set enrichment analysis. Results and Conclusion: The pipeline is described and tested on two benchmark data sets of the haploid S. Cerevisiae ionome and of the human HeLa cell ionome.","authors":[{"name":"Glen R.C."},{"name":"Griffin J.L."},{"name":"Iacovacci J."},{"name":"Lin W."}],"date":"2021-10-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Metabolomics","title":"IonFlow: a galaxy tool for the analysis of ionomics data sets"},"pmcid":"PMC8464566","pmid":"34562172"}],"topic":[{"term":"Cell biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2229"},{"term":"Epigenomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3173"},{"term":"Plant biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0780"},{"term":"Proteomics experiment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3520"},{"term":"Workflows","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0769"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"IonFlow","home":"https://bio.tools/ionflow","license":"Not licensed","summary":"Galaxy tool for processing and analysis of ionomics data , based on the modification of R package IonFlow.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:ionflow/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":true,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":true,"license":false,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":false,"osi":false},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":2,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2022"},{"count":1,"year":"2024"}],"doi":"10.1007/s11306-021-01841-z","pmcid":"PMC8464566","pmid":"34562172","ref_count":23,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"1998"},{"count":1,"year":"2005"},{"count":1,"year":"2006"},{"count":1,"year"